{"schema_version":"1.0","language":"en","edition":"en-ak","revision":"0","book":{"position":19,"code":"PSA","name":"Psalms","testament":"OT"},"chapter":64,"content":[{"type":"para","marker":"d","content":["To the chief Musician, A Psalm of David. "]},{"type":"para","marker":"p","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"1","sid":"PSA 64:1"},"Hear my voice, O God, in my prayer: preserve my life from fear of the enemy. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:1"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"2","sid":"PSA 64:2"},"Hide me from the secret counsel of the wicked; from the insurrection of the workers of iniquity: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:2"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"3","sid":"PSA 64:3"},"Who whet their tongue like a sword, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["and"]}," bend ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["their bows to shoot"]}," their arrows, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["even"]}," bitter words: ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:3"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"4","sid":"PSA 64:4"},"That they may shoot in secret at the perfect: suddenly do they shoot at him, and fear not. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:4"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"5","sid":"PSA 64:5"},"They encourage themselves ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["in"]}," an evil matter: they commune of laying snares privily; they say, Who shall see them? ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:5"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"6","sid":"PSA 64:6"},"They search out iniquities; they accomplish a diligent search: both the inward ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["thought"]}," of every one ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["of them,"]}," and the heart, ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["is"]}," deep. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:6"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"7","sid":"PSA 64:7"},"But God shall shoot at them ",{"type":"char","marker":"add","content":["with"]}," an arrow; suddenly shall they be wounded. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:7"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"8","sid":"PSA 64:8"},"So they shall make their own tongue to fall upon themselves: all that see them shall flee away. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:8"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"9","sid":"PSA 64:9"},"And all men shall fear, and shall declare the work of God; for they shall wisely consider of his doing. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:9"}]},{"type":"para","marker":"q1","content":[{"type":"verse","marker":"v","number":"10","sid":"PSA 64:10"},"The righteous shall be glad in the LORD, and shall trust in him; and all the upright in heart shall glory. ",{"type":"verse","marker":"v","eid":"PSA 64:10"}]}]}
